1. ldpc 2.4.1 (C++ decoder headers)
-----------------------------------

Upstream:  https://github.com/quantumgizmos/ldpc, commit d3429964cd4ffe1abfc041c6ec8b8425cb174f40
           (v2.4.1 era, 2025-12-08)
Licence:   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 Joschka Roffe (full text below)

Where it is used:
  - verify/reference/ldpc/src_cpp/*.hpp: the reference decoder of the verification suite, built
    by verify/reference/CMakeLists.txt behind the C ABI shim verify/reference/ldpc_ref_abi.cpp.
  - src/third_party/ldpc/src_cpp/*.hpp: the same files, byte for byte; the GPU and CPU decoder
    cores compile against them (ldpc's OSD decoder handles osd_cs and osd_e, and the OSD-0 shots
    whose syndrome is outside the image of H), so code from them is part of every decoder core
    built from this tree.

Modified: yes. The changes of verify/reference/ldpc-2.4.1-decoder-bench.patch are applied to the
headers in both directories: an explicit total order for the OSD column sort (soft value
ascending, ties by ascending column index, NaN after every number) and for the LSD candidate
orders, and a fixed shuffle seed, so the post-processing is reproducible. BP itself is unchanged.
Upstream's include/rapidcsv (used only by upstream's C++ unit tests) is not included.

Upstream's src_cpp/sort.hpp marks two index-sort helpers as modified from a Stack Overflow answer
(https://stackoverflow.com/a/36714204); they are part of upstream ldpc and are distributed here as
upstream distributes them.

The licence files of this component are verify/reference/LICENSE and src/third_party/ldpc/LICENSE
(identical), with verify/reference/NOTICE and src/third_party/ldpc/NOTICE.

