3. NVIDIA CUDA runtime (in binaries built from this source)
-----------------------------------------------------------

This source tree contains no NVIDIA code. A build with CUDA (the default; not the CPU-only build
of ELDPC_WITHOUT_CUDA) links the CUDA runtime library of the CUDA Toolkit it is built with
statically (CUDA_RUNTIME_LIBRARY Static, CUDA::cudart_static) into each of the four GPU decoder
cores: libeldpc_core_avx2.so, libeldpc_core_avx512.so, libeldpc_core_avx2_ada64.so and
libeldpc_core_avx512_ada64.so (docs/BUILD.md, "Static CUDA runtime"). The C API front libeldpc.so
and the CPU cores libeldpc_cpu_avx2.so and libeldpc_cpu_avx512.so contain no CUDA runtime. The
NVIDIA driver libraries (libcuda.so.1, libnvidia-ml.so.1) are loaded from the system at run time
and are not distributed.

The CUDA runtime is governed by the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit End User License Agreement
(https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/index.html), not by the Apache License of eldpc. Anyone who
redistributes binaries built from this source (for example a wheel) must comply with that EULA.
